ZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-03-20T09:42:45Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T13:52:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Arch Linux - X11 - Awesome\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04d3f831-2b52-4f1e-96c1-df90488367ff\n\nI think the window works incorrectly on X11. I have an Awesome window manager who allows you to move the windows, which can accidentally move the window, but then it returns back after the movement of the mother window. Moreover, the window border highlight is incorrect at the bottom and right; it becomes fully visible if you move the window away, which means it's a sizing issue. I can also resize the child window, and only after interacting with the main window does it return to its normal state.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI don't know if this applies to X11 in general. But to fix this, simply adjust the main window's size by about 4px from the bottom and right, attach the child window to the main one so that it can't be moved, and prevent manual resizing of the child window.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104400/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104400/timeline","performed_via_git